  @doc "If `runBeforeUnload` is `false`, does not run any unload handlers and waits for the page to be closed. If\n`runBeforeUnload` is `true` the method will run unload handlers, but will **not** wait for the page to close.\n\nBy default, `page.close()` **does not** run `beforeunload` handlers.\n\n**NOTE** if `runBeforeUnload` is passed as true, a `beforeunload` dialog might be summoned and should be handled\nmanually via [`event: Page.dialog`] event.\n\n## Options\n\n  * `:reason` - The reason to be reported to the operations interrupted by the page closure.\n  * `:run_before_unload` - Defaults to `false`."
  @doc since: "v1.8"
  @spec close(t(), keyword()) :: :ok
  def close(page, options \\ []) do
    _ = Playwright.Impl.PageImpl.close(page, CloseOptions.new(options))
    :ok
  end

